 "ellipsis": [],
 "toleranceNote": "Chrome (mock reference) lays text out with integer-rounded glyph advances, Skia with fractional ones: 12-14px text is 2-4% wider in the reference. Only boxes whose width is the text (wrap-content: the meta lines, the FAB, the sort button) depend on that, and what is aligned to their right edge moves with them; every other box is fill/fixed and held to 1px. Search: the chips, the \"Temizle\" button and the \"önizleme\" chip are wrap-content too; the chips after the first move by the sum of the earlier ones' differences, and a title that ends where such a chip starts changes width with it. Downloads: the storage line is `<b>` and `<span class=sub>` inline in one 20px line; Chrome's boxes for them are the inline content areas (18 and 17px), Compose's the 20px line boxes, so their y/h differ by the half-leading (1-1.5px). The legend labels, the \"Hepsini durdur\"/\"Sırala\" buttons and the meta lines are wrap-content text.",
